fix: splash timer resets on each re-render causing infinite stuck splash

Root cause: App.tsx passed an inline arrow function as the `onComplete`
prop to <Splash>. The parent's PremiumTruth context re-renders many
times per second, producing a new function reference on every render.
Splash.tsx's useEffect had [onComplete] as a dependency, so each new
reference restarted the 1400ms countdown — it never completed.

Fix: Splash.tsx now holds `onComplete` in a `useRef` (updated on every
render via a sync effect) and the timer effect uses empty deps `[]` so
the countdown fires exactly once from mount, regardless of parent
re-renders. The error screen in the booting phase now reliably appears
after 1400ms when the backend fails to start.

